# Pairs with DedupNeverDropsNew. Reproduces the receiver half of #1060 as a
# standing check: the drop threshold is the incrementally advanced per-origin
# HWM (the diagonal) instead of the snapshot-pinned floor. Per-leaf clocks are
# unordered, so an origin's HLCs are non-monotonic in delivery order: a writes
# k1 at HLC 2 and then k2 at HLC 1, the receiver applies the first, its HWM
# for a reaches 2, and the second - a genuinely new write to another key - is
# dropped as a duplicate.
MODULE: DedupNeverDropsNewIncrementalDiagonal
TARGET: DedupNeverDropsNew
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: deduplicates on the incremental per-origin HWM, so a new write with a lower HLC to another key is dropped (#1060)
PERTURBS: Deliver

--- FIND
             /\ w.h <= pinned[x][w.o]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the per-origin diagonal is used as a drop threshold.
             /\ w.h <= Max({pinned[x][w.o], hwm[x][w.o]})
--- END
